{"name":"Tumbleweed","hex":"#deaa88","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tumbleweed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant which habitually breaks away from its roots once dry, forming a light, rolling mass which is driven by the wind from place to place; as Russian thistle, wild indigo, witch grass, Amaranthus albus, etc.","One of the dried-out, seed-dispersing, globular forms of such plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumbleweed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tumbleweed","blocks":[{"text":"A tumbleweed is any structural part of the above-ground anatomy of a number of species of plants. It is a diaspore that, once mature and dry, detaches from its root or stem and rolls due to the force of the wind. It is also the name used for these types of plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm/330px--Tumbleweed_in_motion.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumbleweed"},{"title":"Tumbleweed (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Tumbleweed are an Australian rock group formed in 1990 in Tarrawanna. Three of their studio albums appeared on the ARIA top 50: Tumbleweed (1992), Galactaphonic (1995), and Return to Earth (1996)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumbleweed_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/500px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/1280px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg/500px-Tumbleweed_Blooming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young plant blooming in the Mojave Desert in April, after an extremely wet winter season","link":"https: